  <page_number>286</page_number>
  <running_head>EMBLEMATA ET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Fontes</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Nonnunquam Rhodani fluenta tardans</l>
    <l n="2">Dum curfu nimiùm furis tumente:</l>
    <l n="3">Nonnunquam propriis carens &amp; vndis,</l>
    <l n="4">Illum qui rapidis perennitatem</l>
    <l n="5">Largitur fluuiis perenne lauda.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Non funt verba,nec eft loquela</l>
    <l n="7">vobis, Non mens,non ratio,notare docta</l>
    <l n="8">Quæ prudens pietas videt,notátque:</l>
    <l n="9">Sed cùm pergit agens obire munus</l>
    <l n="10">Vnum quodque suum,libénsque paret</l>
    <l n="11">Iustis imperiis heri supremi</l>
    <l n="12">Perscriptáfque tenet vias vicésque</l>
    <l n="13">Immota positas cuique lege:</l>
    <l n="14">Tunc quicquid tegitur polo micante,</l>
    <l n="15">Tunc quicquid geritur solo patente,</l>
    <l n="16">Et quicquid latitat mari profundo,</l>
    <l n="17">Numen concelebrat,canitque summum:</l>
    <l n="18">Cuius cuncta manu manent vigentque:</l>
    <l n="19">Cuius robore stant caduntque cuncta:</l>
    <l n="20">Et cuius sapiens amussis omnes</l>
    <l n="21">Aptè difpositos regit recessus,</l>
    <l n="22">Supremis positos plagis vel imis.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Sed quid sensibus extimis</l>
    <l n="24">Tantùm persequor obuia?</l>
    <l n="25">Eia mens,tibi credita</l>
    <l n="26">Large munera ne sile:</l>
    <l n="27">Quæ non auribus accipi,</l>
    <l n="28">Cerni non oculis queunt:</l>
    <l n="29">Sola sed face luminis</l>
    <l n="30">Interni,radius velut</l>
    <l n="31">Cùm reflexus eò redit,</l>
    <l n="32">Primos vnde trahens suæ</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Faint show-through from the reverse page in the right margin and centre (fragments such as "ontes", "Dic", "Adde" etc.) is not transcribed. Text of the final lines is set in the second column of the verse; "Fontes" is a catchword.</notes>
</page>
